From f4b84b7ad5b17ae4c4e0ac01018c61d14847ffe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: imx471 TEMP DIAG (0079) -- redo full bus scan, correct
 VANA + 400kHz

Re-applies the 0075 in-driver full-bus scan (reverted by 0076), because
both previous scans are now known to have run under broken conditions and
neither can be trusted:

  0070 -- ran with the CCI1 controller clock at 19.2MHz against a timing
          table calibrated for 37.5MHz (fixed later by 0072), and with
          VANA inverted.
  0075 -- ran with the clock corrected, but still with VANA inverted by
          patch 0060: gpio156 was declared GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW, so enabling
          the regulator drove the pin low and switched the sensor's
          analog rail OFF for the whole scan. Fixed by 0077.

Both scans thus swept the address space with the sensor unpowered, which
is why only the EEPROM at 0x50/0x58 -- fed from always-on pm8008_l4 VIO,
not VANA -- ever answered. Their silence says nothing about the sensor.

This run is the first with VANA actually asserted during the window
(verified live: gpio156 observed toggling low->high across a rebind) and
the first at an in-spec 400kHz (0078).

Note a userspace i2cdetect cannot substitute for this: outside the
driver's power window the regulator is disabled and VANA is off, so the
sensor is unpowered for any scan run from the shell. It has to happen
inside imx471_power_on().

Temporary. Revert once the sensor is identified or ruled out.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
index 8cca49580..4f48f75b6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
@@ -576,6 +576,29 @@ static int imx471_power_on(struct device *dev)
 	 * app doesn't stall for 3s once the hardware is sorted. */
 	usleep_range(50000, 60000);
 
+	/* TEMP DIAGNOSTIC (0075, remove once camera works): the 0070 scan
+	 * above ran while the CCI1 clock was still misconfigured at 19.2MHz
+	 * instead of the 37.5MHz the CCI v2 timing table assumes (fixed in
+	 * patch 0072) -- so that scan's silence is not trustworthy evidence
+	 * of a dead bus. Redo it now, fully powered/clocked/reset-released,
+	 * with the corrected clock rate, and log every address that ACKs. */
+	{
+		struct i2c_client *client = to_i2c_client(dev);
+		struct i2c_adapter *adap = client->adapter;
+		int addr;
+
+		dev_info(dev, "imx471 TEMP DIAG (0075): full bus scan while powered, corrected clock\n");
+		for (addr = 0x08; addr <= 0x77; addr++) {
+			union i2c_smbus_data data;
+			int scan_ret = i2c_smbus_xfer(adap, addr, 0,
+						      I2C_SMBUS_READ, 0,
+						      I2C_SMBUS_BYTE, &data);
+			if (scan_ret >= 0)
+				dev_info(dev, "imx471 TEMP DIAG (0075): addr 0x%02x ACKED\n", addr);
+		}
+		dev_info(dev, "imx471 TEMP DIAG (0075): scan complete\n");
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
